    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450-a1">

                <pb facs="1011" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg915"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. De Giers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 14,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith
                    to Your Excellency the petition of Mr. John Calvocoressi, asking that
                    compensation may he made to him by the Imperial Government for the nse of his
                    house and damage to his furniture.</p>
                <p>It appears that Mr. Calvocoressi, an American citizen, was residing temporarily
                    at San Stephano, and that during the occupation of that place his house was
                    taken possession of by the Russian military authorities, and officers quartered
                    there.</p>
                <p>I am instructed by my government to bring this case to Your Excellency’s notice.
                    I trust that compensation will be made to Mr. Calvocoressi for the injury he has
                    suffered. This case appears to be one of peculiar hardship, for not only was
                    occupation maintained during the entire stay of the Russian forces at San
                    Stephano, and his furniture subjected to ordinary use, but unusual damage was
                    done to it, amounting, as can be shown by the officers who occupied the house,
                    to at least £1,500.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
